13:47.548 --> 13:48.530
Nothing.

13:48.532 --> 13:50.982
But how cool is it
I built this?

13:50.984 --> 13:53.819
It's even got a guest room
for the Alan birds.

13:53.821 --> 13:56.204
If you listen real close,
you can hear them.

13:56.206 --> 13:59.024
Cheap, cheap.

14:02.445 --> 14:05.897
♪

14:05.899 --> 14:08.083
(song ends)

14:08.085 --> 14:09.534
Isn't this great?

14:09.536 --> 14:12.737
What's cooler than going
to a strip club in the daytime?

14:12.739 --> 14:15.707
The girls aren't always hot,
but the mozzarella sticks are.

14:16.909 --> 14:19.244
(groans):
Uh... yeah.

14:19.246 --> 14:20.796
You sound like me
two weeks ago.

14:20.798 --> 14:23.465
I made that noise every time
I heard the name "Lyndsey."

14:23.467 --> 14:25.383
(groans)

14:25.385 --> 14:26.818
Yeah, that's it.

14:26.820 --> 14:28.203
What's going on?

14:28.205 --> 14:30.088
To be honest, I, uh...

14:30.090 --> 14:32.423
had a bit of a
breakup myself.

14:32.425 --> 14:33.642
Oh, geez.
Mm.

14:33.644 --> 14:35.894
And here I am whining
about &lt;i>my&lt;/i> problems.

14:35.896 --> 14:37.362
Eh.
I'm sorry, Jeff.

14:37.364 --> 14:39.064
If I have a flaw,
it's that sometimes

14:39.066 --> 14:41.533
I'm not aware of things
that are going on around me.

14:41.535 --> 14:45.587
It's actually one of the
things I like most about you.

14:45.589 --> 14:47.405
So, what happened
between you and your girl?

14:47.407 --> 14:49.291
Well, she wanted
to get married,

14:49.293 --> 14:51.276
and I'm just not
sure I'm ready.

14:51.278 --> 14:53.662
No way! That's the same
reason I lost Lyndsey.

14:53.664 --> 14:55.881
It's like we were
dating the same woman.

14:55.883 --> 14:58.583
It's exactly like that.

14:58.585 --> 15:00.785
So, do you miss her?
Are you kidding?

15:00.787 --> 15:02.287
I mean, she's the
only one for me.

15:02.289 --> 15:05.056
I mean, she's the one who
brings me up when I'm down...

15:05.058 --> 15:08.393
Whoa. Hello, future
Mrs. Strongman.

15:08.395 --> 15:10.462
So, what are you
afraid of?

15:10.464 --> 15:12.731
I don't know.
It's just such a big commitment.

15:12.733 --> 15:14.566
Bottom line:
do you still love her?

15:14.568 --> 15:16.835
Yes, I do.

15:16.837 --> 15:18.136
Then you got to
get her back.

15:18.138 --> 15:19.421
Don't make
the same mistake I did.

15:19.423 --> 15:20.472
Yeah, maybe you're right.

15:20.474 --> 15:22.023
I know I'm right.
Chances like this

15:22.025 --> 15:23.792
only come along
once in a lifetime.

15:23.794 --> 15:25.494
I'm gonna do it, Larry.

15:25.496 --> 15:27.913
I am gonna ask her to marry me.

15:27.915 --> 15:29.331
That-a-boy! And when
things work out,

15:29.333 --> 15:31.917
I'm gonna be the best man
at you and your girl's wedding.

15:31.919 --> 15:35.670
Well... we'll cross that
bridge when we come to it.

15:36.455 --> 15:37.956
Want a private
dance?

15:37.958 --> 15:41.009
Oh, sorry, I can't.
I have a date with destiny.

15:41.011 --> 15:43.211
Destiny's off today.

15:43.213 --> 15:45.714
Oh, no, I-I meant, uh, uh...
Never mind.

15:45.716 --> 15:48.216
Why don't you take my friend.
It's on me.

15:48.218 --> 15:49.834
Oh, I only have a 20.

15:49.836 --> 15:51.553
Uh, you know what?

15:51.555 --> 15:53.939
I think seven's fair.

15:57.109 --> 15:59.294
(machine buzzing)

16:01.631 --> 16:03.148
Walden?

16:03.150 --> 16:04.816
Oh, hey!

16:04.818 --> 16:06.401
Sorry, ladies!

16:06.403 --> 16:08.570
(machine stops)
Man at work!

16:08.572 --> 16:10.055
Wh-What are you doing?

16:10.057 --> 16:14.326
Well, it's a little technical
for the layperson.

16:14.328 --> 16:16.861
What the hell, let me
walk you through it.

16:16.863 --> 16:19.898
What I'm doing is
sanding and re-staining,

16:19.900 --> 16:22.667
when I recognized some
dry rot and termite damage.

16:22.669 --> 16:24.869
And I thought to myself,
what the hell,

16:24.871 --> 16:26.537
I got a couple hours--

16:26.539 --> 16:29.975
why don't I just rebuild
this bad boy from scratch.

16:31.477 --> 16:33.044
(giggles)

16:33.046 --> 16:35.297
The bubbles tickle my nose.

16:35.299 --> 16:37.515
Okay, you know what? You got
to stop building things.

16:37.517 --> 16:39.100
I was wrong--
you are so manly

16:39.102 --> 16:41.670
that if I were straight, I'd
totally bang your brains out.

16:41.672 --> 16:43.154
Well, of course you would,
sweetheart.

16:43.156 --> 16:44.856
But I'd probably
sleep with you once

16:44.858 --> 16:46.274
and then never call you again.

16:46.276 --> 16:47.492
Hold still, please.

16:48.560 --> 16:50.895
Yep, they're level.
(clears throat)

16:52.665 --> 16:54.716
(machine starts)
Ow!

16:54.718 --> 16:56.918
Aah! Aah!

16:56.920 --> 16:58.486
Mmm.

16:58.488 --> 17:01.923
I'm just gonna rub some dirt
in it and keep going.

17:01.925 --> 17:03.858
Walden! Hey...

17:03.860 --> 17:05.176
What are you doing?

17:05.178 --> 17:06.945
Oh, this? Well,

17:06.947 --> 17:09.381
it's pretty technical
for the layperson.

17:09.383 --> 17:10.849
What the hell, let me just...

17:10.851 --> 17:12.517
No, doesn't matter,
doesn't matter.

17:12.519 --> 17:14.386
Uh, I-I got big news.

17:14.388 --> 17:17.555
I am gonna ask Lyndsey
to marry me.

17:17.557 --> 17:18.974
Are you serious?

17:18.976 --> 17:20.758
Yeah, I just have to get a ring.

17:20.760 --> 17:22.427
I got a ring you could have.

17:22.429 --> 17:24.012
The one I proposed to Zoey with.

17:24.014 --> 17:25.780
I don't know,
that ring didn't work.

17:25.782 --> 17:27.198
Neither do you.

17:27.200 --> 17:28.750
(chuckles):
Touché.

17:28.752 --> 17:32.070
Well, I can't believe my
best friend's getting married.

17:32.072 --> 17:34.189
All right, come on,
bring it in.

17:34.191 --> 17:35.407
Man hug.

17:35.409 --> 17:36.941
Oh. Oh. You smell.

17:36.943 --> 17:38.793
Oh, yeah.
It's awesome, isn't it?

17:38.795 --> 17:40.412
I haven't showered in two days.

17:40.414 --> 17:43.248
That's what guys do--
we stank.

17:44.700 --> 17:46.217
You smell good...

17:46.219 --> 17:47.552
bitch.

17:54.927 --> 17:56.928
Ladies love flowers.

17:56.930 --> 17:58.546
Um...

18:08.858 --> 18:11.109
Oh, hey, Jeff!

18:11.111 --> 18:12.810
Why are you calling me Jeff?

18:12.812 --> 18:14.746
You must be here to see
your friend Larry,

18:14.748 --> 18:16.698
who is also here.

18:16.700 --> 18:19.117
Jeff? What are you
doing here?

18:19.119 --> 18:20.418
(laughs):
Larry!

18:20.420 --> 18:23.254
I-I just, uh, I
came by to-to...

18:23.256 --> 18:25.490
yell at this one
over here

18:25.492 --> 18:27.592
for breaking up with
my friend Larry.

18:27.594 --> 18:30.378
Can you think of a better
reason for me to drop by?

18:30.380 --> 18:32.997
'Cause I certainly can't.

18:32.999 --> 18:35.050
Well, now that you're here, why
don't you have a drink with us.

18:35.052 --> 18:37.969
Oh, I-I'm sure Jeff has
better places to be.

18:37.971 --> 18:39.971
Work, nope.
Girlfriend, nope.

18:39.973 --> 18:41.856
Taste in jewelry, nope.

18:41.858 --> 18:43.641
Here you go.

18:43.643 --> 18:45.293
Bottoms up, Lyndsey.

18:45.295 --> 18:48.229
Not the first time
I've said &lt;i>that&lt;/i> to her.

18:48.231 --> 18:49.514
(groans)

18:49.516 --> 18:51.149
What's this?

18:51.151 --> 18:52.683
A ring?

18:53.486 --> 18:55.186
What's going on?

18:55.854 --> 18:59.491
Yeah, what
&lt;i>is&lt;/i> going on?

18:59.493 --> 19:02.327
Jeff helped me realize
I don't want to lose you.

19:02.329 --> 19:03.712
These last two weeks

19:03.714 --> 19:05.663
have been the worst
in my life.

19:05.665 --> 19:07.048
I don't want to spend

19:07.050 --> 19:08.500
another minute without you.

19:08.502 --> 19:09.718
Okay, I think
she's heard enough.

19:09.720 --> 19:11.302
Let's go get some
wings. Come on.

19:11.304 --> 19:12.537
Ooh, wings.

19:12.539 --> 19:14.672
Just let me
wrap this up real quick.

19:16.675 --> 19:19.877
Lyndsey MacElroy,
you're my soul mate.

19:19.879 --> 19:21.996
Will you marry me?

19:21.998 --> 19:23.481
I can't believe
this is happening.

19:23.483 --> 19:25.767
Yes, yes, I will marry you!

19:28.487 --> 19:31.473
So, Jeff, how'd it go
with &lt;i>your&lt;/i> girl?

19:31.475 --> 19:32.824
Uh...

19:32.826 --> 19:34.492
I was too late.

19:34.494 --> 19:36.528
She's marrying someone else.

19:36.530 --> 19:39.164
That was quick.
Wasn't it?

19:39.166 --> 19:41.232
I'm sorry.

19:41.234 --> 19:43.568
LARRY: You know what?
Forget her.

19:43.570 --> 19:47.505
If she chose some jackass over
you, she's just a dumb whore.

19:48.958 --> 19:51.092
Uh, she's-she's
actually really great.

19:51.094 --> 19:52.210
No, she's not.

19:52.212 --> 19:55.447
She and her new man
are both garbage.

19:55.449 --> 19:56.965
(groans):
Uh...

19:56.967 --> 19:58.916
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:08.871 --> 20:10.839
Whoa, look at this.

20:10.841 --> 20:12.838
That's right.

20:12.839 --> 20:13.482
Hey, uh,

20:13.483 --> 20:15.216
who has one and a half thumbs

20:15.218 --> 20:17.585
and built this deck
all by himself?

20:17.587 --> 20:19.704
This guy.

20:19.706 --> 20:21.172
Well, I'm impressed.

20:21.174 --> 20:23.124
I would've had
to call a guy.

20:23.126 --> 20:24.959
Well, then my phone
would've rang,

20:24.961 --> 20:27.045
because I &lt;i>am&lt;/i> the guy.

20:27.047 --> 20:29.247
Got to admit, I was
wrong about you.

20:29.249 --> 20:32.767
That's all right.
We all make mistakes.

20:32.769 --> 20:35.103
Oh! That's my spit cup.

20:36.288 --> 20:39.641
This thing feels sturdy enough
for us to have sex on later.

20:39.643 --> 20:40.809
WALDEN:
Oh, it is.

20:40.811 --> 20:42.143
But, uh, be careful,

20:42.145 --> 20:43.945
'cause I just
stained her.

20:43.947 --> 20:47.148
Well, if you hadn't,
we would have.

20:50.018 --> 20:52.237
Ah. Look at that.

20:52.239 --> 20:55.723
Looks like somebody
needs a new roof.

20:55.725 --> 20:58.159
Luckily, I know a guy.
(chuckles)

20:58.161 --> 21:00.328
(wood crackling)

21:08.551 --> 21:10.518
Whoa. Walden?

21:11.464 --> 21:12.964
WALDEN:
Call a guy!

21:12.966 --> 21:17.966
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
